# Quartz v4 Customization Guide

This guide summarizes how to customize a Quartz v4 website, based on explorations of a typical Quartz project structure.

## 1. Content Authoring

*   **Content Directory**: All Markdown content resides in `/content/`.
*   **Homepage**: The main page is `content/index.md`.
*   **Markdown Flavors**: Supports standard Markdown, GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM), and Obsidian Flavored Markdown (wikilinks, callouts).
*   **Frontmatter**: YAML frontmatter in `.md` files for metadata.
    *   Key fields: `title`, `description`, `permalink`, `aliases`, `tags`, `draft: true` (for private pages), `date` (YYYY-MM-DD).
*   **Recommended Editor**: Obsidian is good for managing links and previews.
*   **Syncing Content**: `npx quartz sync` (if using GitHub for version control/hosting).

## 2. Configuration (`quartz.config.ts`)

This is the primary file for site-wide settings.

*   **Structure**:
    ```typescript
    const config: QuartzConfig = {
      configuration: { /* general settings */ },
      plugins: { /* plugin settings */ },
    }
    ```
*   **General Configuration (`configuration`)**:
    *   `pageTitle`: Site title (e.g., "My Blog").
    *   `baseUrl`: Crucial for deployment (e.g., `username.github.io/repo` or `custom.domain.com`). No `https://` or trailing slashes.
    *   `theme`:
        *   `typography`: Set `header`, `body`, `code` fonts (can use Google Fonts).
            ```typescript
            typography: {
              header: "Schibsted Grotesk",
              body: "Source Sans Pro",
              code: "IBM Plex Mono",
            },
            ```
        *   `colors`: Define color schemes for `lightMode` and `darkMode`.
            ```typescript
            colors: {
              lightMode: {
                light: "#faf8f8",        // Page background
                lightgray: "#e5e5e5",    // Borders
                gray: "#b8b8b8",         // Heavier borders, graph links
                darkgray: "#4e4e4e",     // Body text
                dark: "#2b2b2b",         // Header text, icons
                secondary: "#284b63",    // Link color
                tertiary: "#84a59d",     // Hover states
                highlight: "rgba(143, 159, 169, 0.15)", // Internal link bg, code line highlight
                textHighlight: "#fff23688", // Markdown ==highlight== bg
              },
              darkMode: { /* similar structure */ }
            }
            ```
    *   `analytics`: Configure analytics providers.
    *   `ignorePatterns`: Glob patterns for excluding content.
*   **Plugins (`plugins`)**:
    *   Types: `transformers` (modify content), `filters` (filter content), `emitters` (generate files/pages).
    *   Order matters for transformers.
    *   Add, remove, reorder, and configure plugins here.

## 3. Layout Customization (`quartz.layout.ts`)

Defines the structure of pages using `QuartzComponent`s.

*   **Key Exports**:
    *   `sharedPageComponents`: Layout elements common to all pages (e.g., `head`, `header`, `footer`).
    *   `defaultContentPageLayout`: Layout for single content pages.
    *   `defaultListPageLayout`: Layout for list pages (tags, folders).
*   **Layout Sections**:
    *   `head`: For `<meta>`, `<script>`, `<style>` (invisible).
    *   `header`: Horizontal array of components at the top.
    *   `beforeBody`: Vertical array before main content.
    *   `pageBody`: Main content area (usually `Component.Content()`).
    *   `afterBody`: Vertical array after main content.
    *   `left`: Left sidebar (vertical on desktop/tablet, horizontal on mobile).
    *   `right`: Right sidebar.
    *   `footer`: Footer area.
*   **Example: Removing Left Sidebar & Moving Elements to Header**
    1.  In `sharedPageComponents`, populate the `header`:
        ```typescript
        header: [
          Component.PageTitle(),
          Component.Spacer(),
          Component.Search(),
          Component.Spacer(),
          Component.Darkmode(),
        ],
        ```
    2.  In `defaultContentPageLayout` and `defaultListPageLayout`, empty the `left` array:
        ```typescript
        left: [],
        ```
*   **Available Components**: See `./quartz/components/index.ts` or Quartz documentation for a list (e.g., `PageTitle`, `Search`, `Darkmode`, `Explorer`, `Graph`, `TableOfContents`, `Breadcrumbs`, `ArticleTitle`, `ContentMeta`, `TagList`, `Footer`, `Spacer`).

## 4. Styling

*   **Basic Styling**: Done via `theme` in `quartz.config.ts` (colors, fonts).
*   **Advanced Styling**: Uses Sass.
    *   Base styles: `quartz/styles/base.scss`.
    *   Custom styles: Add to `quartz/styles/custom.scss`.
    *   Component-specific styles might be in `quartz/components/styles/`.
*   **Layout Breakpoints**: Configurable in `quartz/styles/variables.scss` (for `mobile`, `desktop` views).

## 5. Build & Preview

*   **Local Preview**: `npx quartz build --serve`
    *   Starts a hot-reloading server (usually `http://localhost:8080`).
*   **Production Build**: `npx quartz build`
    *   Generates static files in the `public/` directory.
*   **Build Options**:
    *   `--directory`: Content folder (default: `content`).
    *   `--output`: Output folder (default: `public`).

## 6. Deployment

*   Static files from `public/` can be hosted on any static hosting provider.
*   **Key File**: `docs/hosting.md` in the Quartz repo (or official docs site) provides detailed guides for:
    *   Cloudflare Pages
    *   GitHub Pages (requires a GitHub Actions workflow, e.g., `quartz/.github/workflows/deploy.yml`)
    *   Vercel (may need `vercel.json` for clean URLs)
    *   Netlify
    *   GitLab Pages
    *   Self-hosting (Nginx, Apache, Caddy configurations)
*   **Crucial Setting**: Ensure `baseUrl` in `quartz.config.ts` is correctly set for your deployment URL.
*   **Sync command**: `npx quartz sync` can often be used to push changes to GitHub, triggering deployment if CI/CD is set up.

## Key Files to Check First:

*   `content/index.md` (Homepage content)
*   `quartz.config.ts` (Site-wide settings, theme, plugins)
*   `quartz.layout.ts` (Page structure, component placement)
*   `quartz/styles/custom.scss` (Custom CSS/Sass rules)
*   The official Quartz documentation: [https://quartz.jzhao.xyz/](mdc:https:/quartz.jzhao.xyz)
